WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
- I had the honor of visiting
the White House last week

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:03.420
to interview the First Lady.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.510
It's still sinking in.

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:10.237
After our chat, Dr. Biden
asked me just casual like,

00:00:10.237 --> 00:00:12.080
"Oh you wanna go see the oval office?"

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.610
And I was like, who says who to that?

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:14.830
No one says no to that.

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.420
And it's kind of overwhelming.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:17.350
See, there we are.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.716
Isn't that so cool (chuckling) so cool.

00:00:19.716 --> 00:00:20.549
(audience chuckling)

00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:21.382
It's never not going to be cool.

00:00:21.382 --> 00:00:23.720
I'm getting it like blown up in my office.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.940
But it's just nice to be in a place

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.920
where really important things happen.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.380
And the President was so welcoming.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.200
And what's crazy is Dr.
Biden told the President

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.030
that my mama was a teacher.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.047
And he immediately didn't
skip a beat, and he goes,

00:00:38.047 --> 00:00:39.610
"Well, let's just call
her, let's call her."

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.110
And I was like, what?

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:42.860
And then he asked for her number,

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.950
and then I look like
such a horrible daughter,

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.000
because no one knows
anyone's number. (chuckling)

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.993
You just know "Mom" in your contacts.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.450
So now the aides are running around

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:57.460
trying to track down my
phone with my assistant.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.857
And I'm stressing, 'cause I'm like,

00:00:58.857 --> 00:00:59.887
"You really don't have to do it.

00:00:59.887 --> 00:01:01.610
"It's so nice."

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:04.080
And I'm literally standing
in the oval office.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.250
The oval office, hmm-mmm,

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.870
just having a conversation
with President Biden

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:10.630
and Dr. Jill Biden while they're trying

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:11.990
to get ahold of my mom.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:15.270
And then I look up and Trisha
shows up with my phone,

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.383
and my musical director is with her.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.660
And y'all look like you were freaking out.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.850
- Well, to be honest, I was just starving.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.640
And I asked Trisha if there's a sandwich,

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.250
and she said they had them
in your dressing room.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.760
So when they came to get Tricia,

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.380
I grabbed your big makeup bag real quick

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.150
thinking I'm gettin' a sandwich.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.220
I never got the sandwich, but
I got to meet the President.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.620
And I'll carry your makeup bag any day.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.651
(audience applauding)
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:36.651 --> 00:01:37.484
- That was amazing!

00:01:37.484 --> 00:01:39.700
I walk up and Jason's
holding a makeup bag,

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:40.533
and it's like...

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:43.210
And it's like, the President's
there, and we're leaving,

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:46.030
and I said, "Oh, President
Biden, this is Trisha."

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.200
And then all of a sudden I see Jason.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.759
I was like, why is Jason
holding a makeup bag?

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:50.592
(everyone laughing)

00:01:50.592 --> 00:01:51.425
Like, what's happening?

00:01:51.425 --> 00:01:52.650
And he just wanted a sandwich.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:53.483
We didn't get that.

00:01:53.483 --> 00:01:58.483
But the President called my
mom the next day, literally.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.380
And my mom answered the phone.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.901
She was like, "Hello"

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:03.906
And he was like, "Hi, I'm Joe Biden."

00:02:03.906 --> 00:02:07.050
(laughing) And I was
like, "What did you say?"

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:09.160
Anyway, so we have her dialed in.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.260
My mom is actually dialed in right now.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.970
So what's up, Mom?

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:14.803
- Sweetheart.

00:02:14.803 --> 00:02:16.110
- [Kelly] Hi!
(audience applauding)

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.640
I know that we've gone over this.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.270
And it was really funny,
'cause I couldn't recall.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:20.140
Everybody kept asking me

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.260
what we talked about in the Oval office.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.627
And I couldn't remember a dang thing.

00:02:23.627 --> 00:02:26.440
And I remember asking you what happened.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.520
Can you tell everybody else?

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:29.990
- Well, first of all,

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:32.140
I almost didn't answer the
phone, because you know

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.800
I don't answer the phone
if I don't know the number.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.587
And sure enough, when I
answered the phone, he said,

00:02:38.587 --> 00:02:40.470
"Hi, this is John Joe Biden."

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.850
And I thought, "What?"

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.029
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:46.590
I mean, I hate to use
the word surreal, but,

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.750
you know he didn't say
President Joe Biden,

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.067
he just said, "This is Joe Biden."

00:02:53.287 --> 00:02:55.970
And I said, "Oh, hi, how are you?"

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:57.360
He says, "I'm fine."

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.583
And then we proceeded to talk about you,

00:03:00.516 --> 00:03:03.560
and how much that he
and his wife love you.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:04.393
- Go on.
(audience chuckling)

00:03:04.393 --> 00:03:05.460
- And they are...

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.680
They do, they think you are very special.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:08.957
- I'm just kidding.

00:03:08.957 --> 00:03:13.380
- And I said, "Yes, I know
that, she's very special."

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.820
And I got to talk to Dr. Jill Biden.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.950
We talked about both being teachers.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:21.380
She's the oldest of five girls,

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:24.190
and I'm the oldest of four girls.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:26.293
And she talked about, you know, her,

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.940
you know, her sisters and growing up.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:33.210
I mean, it was just like
talking to a neighbor.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.600
And it was...

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.670
They just seem like, you
know, everyday people.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.860
And I thought it was very kind of them,

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.500
to call me when they didn't have to.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:44.810
- Well, I miss you.
(audience applauding)

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:46.550
And I was so excited to get to call you.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:48.150
I called you from the White
House, it's pretty cool,

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:49.370
I'm just saying.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.203
- That is.

00:03:50.203 --> 00:03:53.183
I will have to think about
this in the future though,

00:03:54.158 --> 00:03:55.920
I mean, before I should
have thought about this,

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.640
before I agreed to do it,

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.940
because I haven't had makeup
on now for months and months.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:03.690
- You're beautiful!!

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:04.980
- So I went in there,

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.700
and I looked at my makeup drawer,

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.690
and I thought, where do I start?

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.740
I don't remember.
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:14.070
- Welcome to COVID times. (chuckling)

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.973
- So I thought, "Ah..."

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.083
- You look beautiful.

00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:20.140
- So I apologize to everybody,

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.980
but this what it looks like

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.060
when you haven't had makeup on it a while.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.300
And you forget what goes where, and...

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.580
- Ma'am, that is what it looks
like when you are beautiful,

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.470
and you own it (snapping fingers)

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.040
like Diane Von Furstenberg.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.380
We're gonna to talk about
that book later this show.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.300
I love you so much.
(audience applauding)

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.118
I do think you look beautiful
and I can't wait to see you.

00:04:37.118 --> 00:04:37.951
- Love you!

00:04:37.951 --> 00:04:39.240
- All right, love you, bye!

